1. Same-day duplicates – currently handled
We have seen cases where the same message is received multiple times on the same day, sometimes around 10 occurrences. From what we have checked, the current ingestion deduplication is handling this scenario.
2. Cross-day duplicates – needs BICoE verification
The more important case is where the original message arrives on one day and the same message is replayed on a later day with a different Event Hub enqueuedTime.
This appears capable of escaping our ingestion-stage deduplication and progressing into DLT/Silverish.
Can we please verify the current Production processing for this scenario end-to-end:
Event Hub → ingestion deduplication → DLT/Silverish → Silver
Gaurav's cleanup can remove the historical duplicates, but until the upstream replay behaviour is fully understood/addressed, I think we need to monitor this daily and consider whether Silver needs a continuous deduplication/deletion process, rather than treating this only as a one-off cleanup.
3. Same Quote + Message Type with different quoteStep
We are also seeing cases where the same MQSQuoteId + messageType arrives with different quoteStep values.
My current view is that this is more likely a source-data defect rather than a straightforward duplicate, and this needs to be taken back to MQS/Mule for confirmation. However, from the BICoE perspective, it also appears to escape the ingestion deduplication and can result in multiple records progressing into Silverish.
So for scenarios 2 and 3, can we first understand exactly how the current BICoE logic is treating these records in Production and confirm what reaches Silver?
Until the upstream behaviour is resolved, we should also determine whether we need a daily/continuous Silver-level control to identify and remove these records so that duplicates do not continue accumulating downstream.
